// Modeling -> Manage roles -> New. Create these roles (four, after files
// 18-20 added Developer below), each with a table
// filter on 'llm-usage-container' using the DAX expression shown (paste
// just the expression into the filter box for that table, not the role
// name/comment lines).
//
// Test each with Modeling -> View As -> tick the role (and "Other user",
// entering a UPN) BEFORE publishing. In the Power BI Service, assign an
// Entra ID security group to each role via the workspace dataset's
// Security settings — group-based, not per-user.

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// Role: Employee
// Sees only their own usage.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
[customDimension2] = USERPRINCIPALNAME()
// NOT [appId]: that field holds an APIM subscription id/custom app
// string, never a UPN, so filtering on it here would match nobody.
// [customDimension2] IS the right field — the active
// frag-set-llm-usage.xml fragment now defaults it to a UPN-shaped claim
// (preferred_username/upn/email) from the caller's validated JWT when no
// access contract already set it to something else — see
// guides/power-bi-dashboard.md's "Individual-user page" section. A
// request with no validated JWT still gets "NA" here, so this role
// correctly shows nothing (not someone else's data) for API-key-only
// traffic — a real, honestly documented limitation, not a leak.
// Optional: right-click the column in the Fields pane -> Rename to "End
// User Id" for readability on visuals — purely cosmetic, this filter
// works against the raw customDimension2 name either way.

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// Role: BudgetHolder
// Sees only the cost center(s) they're authorized for, via the
// AuthorizedCostCenters table from 03-supporting-tables.m.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
[customDimension1] IN
    CALCULATETABLE(
        VALUES(AuthorizedCostCenters[costCenter]),
        AuthorizedCostCenters[upn] = USERPRINCIPALNAME()
    )

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// Role: Admin
// Org-wide, no filter — assign to Platform Administrators and Executives
// alike (both are "consume everything" personas in the PRD; split into
// two roles later only if you need genuinely different page access, not
// just different data scope).
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
TRUE()

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// Role: Developer  (added alongside files 18-20)
// Sees only the app(s)/agent(s) they own, via the AuthorizedApps table
// from 19-developer-role.m — a different scope shape than BudgetHolder
// (app ownership, not cost center), since one developer's apps can span
// multiple cost centers and one cost center has many developers.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
[appId] IN
    CALCULATETABLE(
        VALUES(AuthorizedApps[appId]),
        AuthorizedApps[upn] = USERPRINCIPALNAME()
    )
// Apply the same filter shape to GatewayPerformanceLog (file 18):
// [AppId] IN CALCULATETABLE(VALUES(AuthorizedApps[appId]), AuthorizedApps[upn] = USERPRINCIPALNAME())
// 18-failures-latency-source.md's KQL now projects AppId (aliased from
// ApimSubscriptionId) specifically so this applies to the failure/
// latency page too, not just the Cosmos-backed pages — add this as a
// second table filter on the GatewayPerformanceLog table within the
// same Developer role (Manage roles lets one role filter multiple
// tables).
